1
00:00:02,650 --> 00:00:05,850
This Pua motif is known as Tangga Beji (Beji’s Ladder).

2
00:00:06,470 --> 00:00:09,970
This design features a variety of motifs created using the ikat technique applied to the warp threads

3
00:00:10,050 --> 00:00:14,430
This design features a variety of motifs created using the ikat technique applied to the warp threads.

4
00:00:20,950 --> 00:00:25,890
This motif is known as Pucuk Rebung (Bamboo Shoot),

5
00:00:26,950 --> 00:00:31,610
while this section is called Kaki Kemebai Bejalai (Crawling Centipede Legs).

6
00:00:33,650 --> 00:00:37,520
This is the tip of the wood,

7
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:42,360
while this represents Beji climbing the tree.

8
00:00:43,270 --> 00:00:46,820
The reason Beji wanted to climb to the heavens [was to reach the gods],

9
00:00:46,900 --> 00:00:53,300
but this tree, it was an Entepung tree that Beji used back then.

10
00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:58,380
The reason he wanted to climb to the heavens was to follow his brother, Sumping,

11
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:03,170
because Sumping had gone up to the heavens before Beji.

12
00:01:03,250 --> 00:01:07,290
But Sumping could no longer be reached,

13
00:01:07,370 --> 00:01:10,920
because he jumped right off the edge of the sky (nyumping tisi langit).

14
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:14,500
We actually have a pua pattern of Sumping at our longhouse over there.

15
00:01:14,580 --> 00:01:20,060
The motif in this section depicts Beji as

16
00:01:22,150 --> 00:01:26,870
he nearly reaches the sky. However,

17
00:01:26,950 --> 00:01:31,250
the entepung tree breaks because it is too fragile.

18
00:01:31,550 --> 00:01:37,420
The tree collapsed, causing Beji to tumble

19
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:41,000
down through the wind.

20
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:46,420
The broken tree fell

21
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:49,920
and turned into stone,

22
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,420
forming rock formations in the area.

23
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:55,420
Beji was almost at the heavens,

24
00:01:55,500 --> 00:01:57,720
but eventually fell back to earth,

25
00:01:57,800 --> 00:02:01,320
tumbling upside down.

26
00:02:02,700 --> 00:02:04,700
Saddened by the incident,

27
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:08,923
a celestial being named
Endo Segadok sent down

28
00:02:08,947 --> 00:02:12,870
a motif known as Buah
Kelekuh Ambun Belabuh,

29
00:02:12,950 --> 00:02:15,870
Nyawa Rerauh Minta Tutuh Ke Raja Nyaduh,

30
00:02:15,950 --> 00:02:20,420
Buah Engeramuh, Mansau Sedan, Nurun ka Buah Kelekit Gajai Langit,

31
00:02:20,500 --> 00:02:23,220
Nyawa Sesengit Minta Tumbit Ke Raja Tindit,

32
00:02:23,300 --> 00:02:25,120
Bukit Tumpur Nyadi Emperan.

33
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:28,120
The Tangga Beji motif

34
00:02:28,200 --> 00:02:31,120
was first woven by Dayang Kerja,

35
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:35,120
the wife of Sumbang Berani.

36
00:02:40,050 --> 00:02:45,190
Initially, I had no samples or references to guide me

37
00:02:45,270 --> 00:02:48,920
in creating the Tangga Beji weaving.

38
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:51,050
Therefore, I developed the motif

39
00:02:51,130 --> 00:02:53,020
based on my own inspiration.

40
00:02:53,100 --> 00:02:56,230
The Tangga Beji motif was developed

41
00:02:56,310 --> 00:03:00,310
from my own ideas and creativity.

42
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:15,000
That was the story behind the Tangga Beji motif.

43
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:20,900
This textile is woven using silk threads dyed with natural dyes.

44
00:03:20,950 --> 00:03:26,110
such as the red dye extracted from the roots of the mengkudu plant.

45
00:03:26,650 --> 00:03:29,300
I insisted that I wouldn't use chemical dyes (selup);

46
00:03:29,380 --> 00:03:33,320
all the pua I make, none of them use chemical dye or synthetic dye (selup / dye).

47
00:03:33,400 --> 00:03:35,570
This textile uses natural colours

48
00:03:35,650 --> 00:03:38,600
derived from sources such as mengkudu roots.

49
00:03:38,680 --> 00:03:42,330
Engkudu dye does not easily fade even when the fabric is washed to water.

50
00:03:42,410 --> 00:03:46,910
The process of obtaining the red
colour from mengkudu roots

51
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:51,500
is repeated eight times to achieve the
desired colour intensity and quality.

52
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:54,000
I cooked it for an hour and a half.

53
00:03:56,050 --> 00:04:00,815
The blue colour is obtained
using natural dye extracted

54
00:04:00,839 --> 00:04:05,250
from renggat leaves, also
known as tarum leaves.

55
00:04:05,700 --> 00:04:08,620
A second round of motif binding

56
00:04:08,700 --> 00:04:12,670
is carried out to create the blue-coloured motifs.

57
00:04:12,750 --> 00:04:15,750
Once the dyeing process is complete,

58
00:04:16,570 --> 00:04:18,770
the raffia string bindings are removed.

59
00:04:18,850 --> 00:04:21,000
In the past, lemba leaves

60
00:04:21,080 --> 00:04:24,120
were used to bind the motifs.

61
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:28,500
However, they have now been replaced with raffia strings coated with wax.

62
00:04:29,150 --> 00:04:31,570
The raffia string must

63
00:04:31,650 --> 00:04:34,570
be tightly wrapped and twisted around the threads

64
00:04:34,650 --> 00:04:36,670
to ensure a neat and well-defined pattern.

65
00:04:38,400 --> 00:04:42,980
This is how I tie the motifs.

66
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:48,820
It took me about a month

67
00:04:48,900 --> 00:04:52,770
to complete the Tangga Beji textile,

68
00:04:52,850 --> 00:04:55,770
starting from the ngirit (warp preparation) process.

69
00:04:55,850 --> 00:04:58,770
The drying time of the threads

70
00:04:58,850 --> 00:05:03,390
depends on the weather conditions.

71
00:05:03,850 --> 00:05:06,900
To create the blue colour,

72
00:05:06,980 --> 00:05:09,520
the threads are tied for a second time

73
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:18,060
before being dyed using renggat leaves.

74
00:05:19,400 --> 00:05:22,400
This Tangga Beji textile can be washed

75
00:05:25,300 --> 00:05:28,300
just like any other fabric.

76
00:05:31,550 --> 00:05:35,190
Although I had heard the story of Tangga Beji,

77
00:05:35,270 --> 00:05:40,120
I had never seen anyone in our longhouse create this weaving.

78
00:05:40,200 --> 00:05:44,570
Therefore, I took the initiative to develop the motif based on my own inspiration,

79
00:05:44,650 --> 00:05:49,520
so that the story of Beji ascending to the heavens

80
00:05:49,600 --> 00:05:53,300
and Aji, who could not return to the underworld,

81
00:05:53,380 --> 00:05:56,880
would continue to be passed down as a lesson for future generations.

82
00:05:56,960 --> 00:05:58,960
Beji wanted to follow his brother

83
00:05:58,999 --> 00:06:05,279
but mistakenly chose an entepung tree, which was not sturdy enough.

84
00:06:05,650 --> 00:06:09,650
I do not copy others' work.

85
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:17,000
This Sungai Kain version of the Tangga Beji motif

86
00:06:17,950 --> 00:06:20,870
is entirely my own design and weaving.

87
00:06:20,950 --> 00:06:24,270
I created this motif

88
00:06:24,350 --> 00:06:29,170
as a moral lesson,

89
00:06:29,250 --> 00:06:32,420
illustrating Beji’s determination

90
00:06:32,500 --> 00:06:36,200
to follow his eldest brother,

91
00:06:36,280 --> 00:06:37,330
Aji.

92
00:06:37,450 --> 00:06:41,470
Beji wanted to ascend to the heavens

93
00:06:41,550 --> 00:06:48,570
because Aji could not return to earth.

94
00:06:48,650 --> 00:06:50,770
According to the elders’ stories,

95
00:06:50,850 --> 00:06:55,420
this tale portrays the bond

96
00:06:55,500 --> 00:06:59,420
between siblings.

97
00:06:59,500 --> 00:07:02,420
I have long wanted

98
00:07:02,500 --> 00:07:07,870
to create this Tangga Beji motif.

99
00:07:07,950 --> 00:07:13,970
I wove it as a lesson and a legacy so that

100
00:07:14,050 --> 00:07:18,620
its story and meaning will be remembered by my children,

101
00:07:18,700 --> 00:07:21,620
grandchildren and future generations,

102
00:07:21,700 --> 00:07:26,670
even after I am gone.

103
00:07:26,750 --> 00:07:32,470
I am truly grateful that you chose the story of Tangga Beji

104
00:07:32,550 --> 00:07:35,550
from all the Pua Kumbu I have created.

105
00:07:39,750 --> 00:07:43,720
I wove the Tangga Beji motif

106
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:47,320
as a lesson and reminder,

107
00:07:47,400 --> 00:07:52,220
so that future generations

108
00:07:52,300 --> 00:07:56,900
will remember Beji’s longing for his brother, Aji.

109
00:07:56,980 --> 00:08:00,580
I created the Tangga Beji motif

110
00:08:00,660 --> 00:08:03,520
based on my own understanding

111
00:08:03,600 --> 00:08:07,260
and inspiration

112
00:08:07,750 --> 00:08:13,020
to preserve the stories

113
00:08:13,100 --> 00:08:16,020
of the elders

114
00:08:16,100 --> 00:08:20,770
as a reminder

115
00:08:20,850 --> 00:08:25,850
for future generations.

